== S2  the consumed instances, rewritten as statements about tables
PASS S2.rot  [identity] Rz(m1), Rx(m2) (rational parametrization of the angles) are rotations: R^T R = I, det R = 1
PASS S2.G7ii  [identity] cnot (prodState (Rz xplus) (Rx z3)) = actC (Rz Rx) phiW (design G7(ii)), symbolic angles
PASS S2.G7iii  [identity] actC (Rz Rx) phiW = actT (Rx Rz) phiW (design G7(iii)), symbolic angles
PASS S2.loc  [identity] actC M (prodState u v) = prodState (M u) v and actT M (prodState u v) = prodState u (M v), symbolic
PASS S2.L  [identity] (L): N (prodState u v) = actC A actT B cnot (prodState (A' u) (B' v)) for N-CLASS N, symbolic; with u = A'^T Rz xplus, v = B'^T Rx z3 and A' A'^T = B' B'^T = I this is actC (A Rz Rx) (actT B phiW)
PASS S2.BS  [identity] (BS): at m1 = m2 = 0 the link table is bellOf A B = actC A (actT B phiW)
PASS S2.BE  [identity] (BD): tens (sharpVec u) (sharpVec v) = 1/4 prodState u v, symbolic, so the gate image of the sharp product consumed by bell_mem_dual is 1/4 bellOf A B
PASS S2.Bc  [countercontrol] countercontrol: with phiW replaced by idW, (BS) at the M_D post-local B = reflY is not the M_Q Bell table (the post-local is read: actT reflY phiW = idW differs from phiW)

